| ma-g8-craft (assigned roles, a bent convention, adapted tools and content) | ma-g9-craft | 3 | The student chooses the role and takes a risk on purpose against a set constraint |
| ma-g8-present (a theme across formats, an improvement put in place) | ma-g9-present | 5 | A collection, not a single piece, designed for varied audiences |
| ma-g8-read (parts and styles contrasted) | ma-g9-read | 2 | Artists' choices read, and more than one sense considered |
| ma-g8-judge (built criteria against goals and context) | ma-g9-judge | 4 | The student's own work judged at key production stages, not only when finished |
| ma-g8-society (civic and environmental values, legal and online limits) | ma-g9-society | 2 | Power, equality, identity and digital identity, and the career side of media work |
| ma-g8-sources (cultural knowledge and model works guide the making) | ma-g9-sources | 5 | Outside sources and the student's own woven into one original piece |

### Inside the band: level to level

Each row of Levels 2 to 4 assumes the level before's row in its thread (one year back when the levels are taken in
turn), so it opens as a retrieval task inside day 2 of its unit; the review units (6, 11) hold the readiness check
and the placement for a student who skipped a year or places in.

| Thread | Level 1 row (unit, band days) | Level 2 row (unit) | Level 3 row (unit) | Level 4 row (unit) | What changes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ideas | ma-g9-ideas (unit 3, days 43 to 76) | ma-g10-ideas (unit 8): methods chosen on purpose, the student's own aesthetic within resource limits | ma-g11-ideas (unit 13): design principles with methods, an original framework under complex limits from knowledge of a system | ma-g12-studio (unit 16), with make and craft | Named methods, then strategic methods and a personal aesthetic, then systems and complex limits, then a proposal the student writes |
| Making | ma-g9-make (unit 4, days 79 to 116) | ma-g10-make (unit 9): continuity or juxtaposition, refined for chosen audiences | ma-g11-make (unit 14): hybrid, complex work polished throughout | ma-g12-studio (unit 16) | Emphasis and tone to own goals, then audience impact, then hybridization, then a series |
| Production | ma-g9-craft (unit 3, days 43 to 76) | ma-g10-craft (unit 8): managing a production, exploring after failure, interactivity | ma-g11-craft (unit 13): questions framed by the student, a toolset adapted across experimental work | ma-g12-studio (unit 16) | A chosen role and a risk, then managing and failing forward, then framing the question, then the student's own production |
| Presenting | ma-g9-present (unit 5, days 117 to 156) | ma-g10-present (unit 10): a theme across arts, media and school-subject content; a curated collection for a virtual channel | ma-g11-present (unit 15): work that holds across platforms; a promoted showing aimed at a real effect, results compared | ma-g12-exhibit (unit 19) | A collection for two audiences, then a curated channel, then a promoted cross-platform showing, then a self-run showing |
| Reading media | ma-g9-read (unit 2, days 13 to 42) | ma-g10-read (unit 7): pieces compared, with audience feedback; persuasion across senses | ma-g11-read (unit 12): many kinds of pieces; top-quality examples steering across systems | ma-g12-criticism (unit 17), with judge | One piece and its maker's choices, then comparison and persuasion, then systems, then an extended defended reading |
| Judging | ma-g9-judge (unit 4, days 79 to 116) | ma-g10-judge (unit 9): purpose and influence across settings; an evaluation defended against an objection | ma-g11-judge (unit 14): bias weighed; a rigorous critique built alone, with feedback sought | ma-g12-criticism (unit 17) | Key production stages, then a defended evaluation, then a bias check, then criteria of more than one kind |
| Media and society | ma-g9-society (unit 2, days 13 to 42) | ma-g10-society (unit 7): commerce, power, propaganda and truth; audience interactivity in the legal and career setting | ma-g11-society (unit 12): personal and worldwide purposes; strategic navigation of systems | ma-g12-purpose (unit 18), with sources | Power and identity, then propaganda and truth, then worldwide purpose, then a real audience with consent and credit |
| Sources | ma-g9-sources (unit 5, days 117 to 156) | ma-g10-sources (unit 10): introspection and research behind a persuasive piece | ma-g11-sources (unit 15): sources sought without being handed over; new knowledge | ma-g12-purpose (unit 18) | Outside and own sources woven, then reflection and research, then independent search, then a record of every source choice |

Level 2 rows sit at band days 167 to 316 (unit 6 days 161 to 166, unit 7 167 to 198, unit 8 199 to 236, unit 9 239
to 276, unit 10 277 to 316); Level 3 rows at band days 327 to 476; Level 4 at band days 481 to 636.

### Handed on: where the threads end

Media Arts, grades 9 to 12 is the last media arts course; its threads end here. Level 3 hands every thread to Level 4
(ma-g11-ideas, ma-g11-make and ma-g11-craft to ma-g12-studio; ma-g11-present to ma-g12-exhibit; ma-g11-read and
ma-g11-judge to ma-g12-criticism; ma-g11-society and ma-g11-sources to ma-g12-purpose). The Level 4 rows hand on
nothing (their hands_on cells are empty). A student who stops after any level leaves with a complete course and a
portfolio: the level's pieces, logs and showing plans, which a later level's placement reads.

## Models carried

All eight come in from grade 8 (the ma-g8 rows' model_out) and are taught again in the bridge as readiness.

| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here |
|---|---|---|---|
| look-describe-interpret | Grade 8 (ma-g8-read, model_out) | Unit 1 (the bridge): describe, interpret, ground in the piece, retaught on one clip; unit 2 uses it for artists' choices and senses (ma-g9-read) | Unit 7 (comparison and persuasion, ma-g10-read), unit 12 (systems, ma-g11-read), unit 17 (the extended reading, ma-g12-criticism); every unit's study day as review |
| media-ethics-check | Grade 8 (ma-g8-society, model_out) | Unit 1: the check card (permission, consent, credit, license of each source, where it may be shown); unit 2 extends it to digital identity and careers (ma-g9-society) | Unit 7 (propaganda, truth and audience interaction, ma-g10-society), unit 12 (worldwide purpose and systems, ma-g11-society), unit 18 (the real-audience project, ma-g12-purpose); every making day as review |
| storyboard | Grade 8 (ma-g8-ideas, model_out) | Unit 1: the storyboard and workflow sheet; unit 3 adds named idea methods and the aesthetic standards list (ma-g9-ideas) | Unit 8 (strategic methods and limits, ma-g10-ideas), unit 13 (a framework under complex limits, ma-g11-ideas), unit 16 (the proposal, ma-g12-studio) |
| production-roles | Grade 8 (ma-g8-craft, model_out) | Unit 1: the role cards (director, camera or capture, sound, editor, producer); unit 3 has the student choose and log a role (ma-g9-craft) | Unit 8 (managing a production, ma-g10-craft), unit 13 (framing the question, ma-g11-craft), unit 16 (every role the student's own choice, ma-g12-studio); every team piece as review |
| revision-log | Grade 8 (ma-g8-make, model_out) | Unit 1: the log of each change and why; unit 4 ties each change to a stated personal goal (ma-g9-make) | Unit 9 (changes for a chosen audience, ma-g10-make), unit 14 (polish throughout, ma-g11-make), unit 16 (the series, ma-g12-studio) |
| critique-protocol | Grade 8 (ma-g8-judge, model_out) | Unit 1: describe, ask, suggest, retaught; unit 4 applies it at two production stages against named criteria (ma-g9-judge) | Unit 9 (a defended evaluation, ma-g10-judge), unit 14 (a bias check and feedback sought, ma-g11-judge), unit 17 (more than one set of criteria, ma-g12-criticism); every critique as review |
| screening-plan | Grade 8 (ma-g8-present, model_out) | Unit 1: the plan card (what, for whom, where, in what order, how the audience meets it); unit 5 plans a collection for two audiences (ma-g9-present) | Unit 10 (a curated channel plan, ma-g10-present), unit 15 (a promotion plan and results, ma-g11-present), unit 19 (the student-run showing, ma-g12-exhibit) |
| source-log | Grade 8 (ma-g8-sources, model_out) | Unit 1: the log (source, holder, license, how used, credit line); unit 5 weighs outside and own sources (ma-g9-sources) | Unit 10 (introspection and research, ma-g10-sources), unit 15 (sources found alone, ma-g11-sources), unit 18 (every source choice recorded, ma-g12-purpose); every made piece credits from it |

