ng: forms blended into one piece with the planned audience moment working; MA:Pr6.1.Ia, the kept collection showing plan: order, two formats and two audiences, how each meets the work; MA:Pr6.1.Ib, a kept written review after the first screening naming one improvement, with the second screening's look-for showing it made, and the gains to self and community weighed; MA:Cn10.1.Ia, the kept source log and credits on the piece: outside sources judged and woven with the student's own (scored at the mid-unit checkpoint on the rough cut); MA:Cn10.1.Ib, a written account on the second check day: how the collection and one online teaching page widen meaning and build culture. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: school-subject content and virtual channels (Level 2). Tools: the screening-plan card, the source log, a program template, Curio Class's own. Free path: a sheet or wall for a screen, printed programs, a live sound score. Short path: 19 days | Last in Level 1 because the collection is built from the level's pieces and the new team piece, and the showing ends the level before the year-end check in week 32. The source log, kept since the bridge, is weighed here for the first time | Candidate: the second audience moved to a community partner's space where the school allows it, with every yes | Native Knowledge 360A�: the sensitivity agent reads the museum's own pages first and the unit uses them as Native educators present them; no student restages a Native practice. Remix: public domain or openly licensed sources only, named on the piece. Showing outside class needs each yes. Hazards and controls: an evening showing in the school's space with the school's own adults; cords taped; no flashing light; headphones low. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
