d by id: MA:Re7.1.IIa, a mid-unit sitting item: how parts relate across three unseen public domain posters, with the class poll's feedback used; MA:Re7.1.IIb, a sitting item on the end check day: how an unseen public domain clip persuades through sight and sound, played twice; MA:Cn11.1.IIa, a guide look-for on the kept two-sided piece: the persuasive piece and its truth panel naming commerce, power, propaganda or truth; MA:Cn11.1.IIb, the kept media-ethics check and a written route through one case card's legal, technical, systemic and career sides, with the audience interaction it raises. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: worldwide purposes and strategic navigation (Level 3). Tools: work cards, case cards, the poll card, Curio Class's own. Free path: paper, markers, cut paper. Short path: 16 days | After the review because analysis and the media-ethics check pick up where Level 1's unit 2 left them; first of the level's paired units because unit 8's interactive piece and unit 10's persuasive piece both need the study of persuasion and audience interaction first | Candidate: a persuasive piece by a living maker from Asia or Africa, described and linked | Hard history and propaganda: some wartime posters used racist caricature; the unit chooses posters without it, says in one plain sentence that such posters were made, and shows none. The Chilean dictatorship's disappeared: the sensitivity agent reads the film's own pages and a Chilean memorial body's published words first; no student is asked about their own family's history. Invented products and causes only; no real brand. Hazards and controls: markers non-toxic; shared devices wiped. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
