int); MA:Re8.1.II, a sitting item on the end check day: an unseen public domain clip's purpose, meaning and influence in two settings; MA:Re9.1.II, a kept written critique of a classmate's piece or a studied piece and its steps, with criteria, evidence and one objection answered. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: hybridization (Level 3). Tools: the revision log, the objection card, Curio Class's own; a work viewer. Free path: paper strip and a live sound score. Short path: 19 days | After mid-year because the individual piece uses unit 8's prototype habits; before unit 10 because the theme piece needs continuity and a chosen audience first, and the defended evaluation feeds the showing's review | Candidate: a third work using collision cuts by a living maker from Asia or Latin America, described and linked | Potemkin's steps sequence shows soldiers firing on a crowd: the teacher previews; the unit shows only the cuts it names and describes the rest; the film is studied as 1925 Soviet state cinema made to persuade. Daughters of the Dust: the sensitivity agent reads the film's own pages and Gullah Geechee Cultural Heritage Corridor pages first; no student imitates Gullah speech or dress. Hazards and controls: headphones low; screen breaks; shared devices wiped. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
