:Pr5.1.8b, a written item: a named problem card and a convention the student would bend to solve it, why; MA:Pr5.1.8c, a written item: how one tool, one method and the content were adapted to the team's intent. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: roles chosen by the student and creative risk (Level 1). Tools: the planning portfolio, the workflow chart, role cards, a sound score sheet, Curio Class's own. Free path: a live found-sound score and a paper animatic. Once-a-week path: 9 sessions | After unit 9 because the team's intent and its sources answer to the legal setting just added; before unit 11 because the style piece is produced through a planned workflow. Longest unit of the year: five ids and a team production | Candidate: a Native American maker who bends a media convention, described and linked, for the year's range | Pumzi shows a future of water scarcity: the unit studies it as a story and a production, without fear tasks; the agent reads the maker's own published words first. Found sound: no recording of people without their yes; volume low; no sudden loud sound in a student's ear. Hazards and controls: headphones at low volume, cords taped, recording only with the family's yes, screen breaks. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
