ten item on the second check day: the results and the improvement actually made, with evidence; MA:Cn10.1.8a, a kept card: the source log, cultural and social knowledge and a model work judged and credited; MA:Cn10.1.8b, a written item on the second check day: how one unseen public domain piece carried a local event to a wider audience. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: a collection for varied audiences (Level 1). Tools: the showing plan, the source log, a work viewer, Curio Class's own. Free path: a printed photo-essay and a live radio version. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | Last in the band because the screening joins the year's workflow, style and legal setting into one theme across formats; the sources thread ends the band at culture and the wider world, handed to Level 1. Its screening and written check end the year's units before the year-end check in week 32 | Candidate: a model work by a living maker from Africa or Asia on a local-to-worldwide event, for range | Vyarawalla's photographs show India's independence, which came with the partition of the country: the agent reads the museum's or archive's page and her published words first, the unit names the partition in one plain sentence and picks photographs of the celebrations and leaders only, with no image of violence. The Moon landing: the unit uses the agency's own pages and dates. A student's chosen event: no family or personal history is required. Hazards and controls: screen breaks, volume low, recording only with the family's yes, family yes for any showing outside class. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
